{"name":"Twice Shy","hex":"#ca999e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"twice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Two times.","Doubled in quantity, intensity, or degree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twice"},{"term":"shy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tachawit. The native name for the Shawiya language."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily frightened; timid.","Reserved; disinclined to familiar approach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Twice","blocks":[{"text":"Twice is a South Korean girl group formed by JYP Entertainment. The group is composed of nine members: Nayeon, Jeongyeon, Momo, Sana, Jihyo, Mina, Dahyun, Chaeyoung, and Tzuyu. They are recognized as one of the best-selling girl groups of all time and are widely regarded as one of K-pop's most influential acts. Twice have been dubbed \"The Nation's Girl Group\" in their home country and are credited for their role in leading the re-emergence of girl groups in the Korean Wave. Initially known for their bright and youthful image, the group has since evolved to explore an array of sounds and concepts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Twice_260618.jpg/330px-Twice_260618.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twice"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Twice_260618.jpg/500px-Twice_260618.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Twice_260618.jpg/1280px-Twice_260618.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Twice_260618.jpg/500px-Twice_260618.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","